{"parentUuid":"ffb5c560-be2d-4b35-a9e8-c725351c3133","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfLPKEsgn9MiuwCxKczGC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MpPfJSEnpNepjCHoKivJXy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_cfb-forecast-capture.md | head -40","description":"Read forecast capture memory note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":83849,"output_tokens":242,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":81},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":242,"cache_read_input_tokens":83849,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":663},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MpPfJSEnpNepjCHoKivJXy":{"command":"cat ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_cfb-forecast-capture.md | head -40","description":"Read forecast capture memory note"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"443a84c9-7f83-49c5-ba4d-6289ea3c6d1c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfLPKEGicB81KkxDJGbxD","attributionSkill":"dev-sync","type":"assistant","uuid":"c90a3eb1-7018-47da-b08a-7e9877f70d37","timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:39:22.542Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model","sessionId":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"c90a3eb1-7018-47da-b08a-7e9877f70d37","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5006fe82-af7e-4da5-9995-ef680c5b9f3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MpPfJSEnpNepjCHoKivJXy","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: cfb-forecast-capture\ndescription: \"CFB Victory Model weekly forecast freeze — all 16 Big 12 teams via scripts/weekly_run.sh, archive mirror, Monday-anchored nag 2026-08-24 to 2027-01-23, no backfill, and how to tell a real missed week from a stale snapshot\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 330c1f71-242a-47c7-ac7b-129bd6f5dd3c\n  modified: 2026-09-02T19:20:41.051Z\n---\n\nThe CFB Victory Model's pre-game forecasts are frozen once per week by the\n`/forecast-capture` skill, which snapshots predictions **before kickoff** and reports what\nmoved since the prior week.\n\n## Scope and entry point (changed 2026-09-02, per Eric)\n\n- **All 16 Big 12 teams every week**, not Baylor only. The list is the `BIG12` constant in\n  `weekly_capture.py` — one home; do not copy team lists into the wrapper or the skill.\n  `--teams`/`--team` still narrow a run. Budget ~10 min for the full sweep.\n- **One entry point:** `~/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/scripts/weekly_run.sh` (capture → compare\n  `--all --archive`). It hardcodes the absolute `uv` path.\n- **Archive mirror:** every snapshot and comparison is copied to\n  `~/DEV/CFB_Forecast_Archive/<season>/`. Read-only copy; truth stays in\n  `CFB_Victory_Model/data/`. Registered in `backup-manifest.json` as `personal`/ssd —\n  see [[backup-sync-system]] for why a new `~/DEV` folder must be added there.\n- The ritual guard still keys off the newest `*_baylor.csv`, which the Big 12 sweep always\n  writes, so detection is unaffected.\n\n## A gap can mean the other machine captured it\n\nConfirmed 2026-09-09. The Mac's `data/weekly_forecast_log.csv` looked like it had\nmissed 2026-08-26 and 2026-08-31 — it jumped 07-31 → 09-02. Neither week was\nmissed. **Both were captured on the Windows box**, which runs the same wrapper\nagainst the same repo. The two machines had diverged, each holding captures the\nother lacked.\n\nBefore declaring a missed week, check the other machine's copy of the log.\nMerging is safe: the natural key is `(captured_at, season, team, week, game_id)`,\nand a union on that key had **zero conflicts** across 216 Mac + 348 Windows rows\n→ 540. Same key never carried different values. See [[github-consolidation]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f2cacc84-156f-421b-8084-aefdc4469dac","timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:39:22.892Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: cfb-forecast-capture\ndescription: \"CFB Victory Model weekly forecast freeze — all 16 Big 12 teams via scripts/weekly_run.sh, archive mirror, Monday-anchored nag 2026-08-24 to 2027-01-23, no backfill, and how to tell a real missed week from a stale snapshot\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 330c1f71-242a-47c7-ac7b-129bd6f5dd3c\n  modified: 2026-09-02T19:20:41.051Z\n---\n\nThe CFB Victory Model's pre-game forecasts are frozen once per week by the\n`/forecast-capture` skill, which snapshots predictions **before kickoff** and reports what\nmoved since the prior week.\n\n## Scope and entry point (changed 2026-09-02, per Eric)\n\n- **All 16 Big 12 teams every week**, not Baylor only. The list is the `BIG12` constant in\n  `weekly_capture.py` — one home; do not copy team lists into the wrapper or the skill.\n  `--teams`/`--team` still narrow a run. Budget ~10 min for the full sweep.\n- **One entry point:** `~/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model/scripts/weekly_run.sh` (capture → compare\n  `--all --archive`). It hardcodes the absolute `uv` path.\n- **Archive mirror:** every snapshot and comparison is copied to\n  `~/DEV/CFB_Forecast_Archive/<season>/`. Read-only copy; truth stays in\n  `CFB_Victory_Model/data/`. Registered in `backup-manifest.json` as `personal`/ssd —\n  see [[backup-sync-system]] for why a new `~/DEV` folder must be added there.\n- The ritual guard still keys off the newest `*_baylor.csv`, which the Big 12 sweep always\n  writes, so detection is unaffected.\n\n## A gap can mean the other machine captured it\n\nConfirmed 2026-09-09. The Mac's `data/weekly_forecast_log.csv` looked like it had\nmissed 2026-08-26 and 2026-08-31 — it jumped 07-31 → 09-02. Neither week was\nmissed. **Both were captured on the Windows box**, which runs the same wrapper\nagainst the same repo. The two machines had diverged, each holding captures the\nother lacked.\n\nBefore declaring a missed week, check the other machine's copy of the log.\nMerging is safe: the natural key is `(captured_at, season, team, week, game_id)`,\nand a union on that key had **zero conflicts** across 216 Mac + 348 Windows rows\n→ 540. Same key never carried different values. See [[github-consolidation]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c90a3eb1-7018-47da-b08a-7e9877f70d37","session_id":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CFB_Victory_Model","sessionId":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
