xternal","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"148b8ac4-1c07-4317-a6f6-932ea3d21267","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5006fe82-af7e-4da5-9995-ef680c5b9f3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016DVPLHFoveuxx8MiWjKMrT","type":"tool_result","content":"AGENTS.md\nCLAUDE.md\n     228 AGENTS.md\n      96 docs/STATUS.md\n     324 total\n2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md\n2026-09-22-db-off-drive-and-parquet-snapshots.md\n# STATUS\n\n## Current state (2026-09-22)\n- **The DB no longer lives in the repo.** `src/db.py` resolves it from **`$PFF_DB`**\n  (Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pff-data\\pff.db`), falling back to `data/pff.db` when unset,\n  so the Mac is unchanged until it sets the variable. Cause: `~/Desktop/DEV` is a two-way\n  Google Drive mirror and Drive re-uploads and **locks** the 542 MB file on every write.\n  `GoogleDriveFS.exe` held it open against a running pull. PR #1.\n- **2026 pulled** (`run_pipeline.py --season 2026`): 1,614 games, 16,572 grades,\n  1,252,863 stats, 39,960 premium; graded weeks 0-3. Baylor: 79 players over its 3\n  played games, 17,215 snaps. Week 4 is 2026-09-26, so 3 games is complete, not a gap.\n- **Machines now exchange Parquet, not databases** (PR #2). `scripts/export_snapshot.py`\n  and `scripts/load_snapshot.py`, one file per table per season on Drive plus a\n  manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full\n  snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\n- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\n  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found, data restored and the script fixed the same night (PR #4).\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n- All 12 PFF API specs saved to `docs/swagger/` (2026-09-13). Eight were new; master-data\n  and grades-feeds were refreshed (both only gained endpoints). The key downloads specs\n  directly: `GET /doc/swagger/<slug>.yaml` with the Bearer JWT.\n- PFF EPA located and verified (2026-09-13): `/v1/video/ncaa/games/{id}/plays` carries\n  `expected_points_added` and `expected_points_added_legacy`, 100% play coverage on\n  Baylor 2024-2026 and six random non-Baylor 2025 games.\n- Video plays ingested for all 25 Baylor 2024-2025 games (2026-09-13): `pff_premium`\n  category `video_plays`, 4,517 rows (both offences), zero missing EPA.\n  `scripts/pull_video_plays.py --season 2024 --season 2025`. Season and week come\n  from the games table: a bowl game's rows carry week \"BG\". Pre-change backup:\n  `data/pff_before_video_plays_20260913_204343.db`.\n- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the\n  games lists, `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py`. Verified against the per-game pull\n  (all 2,215 Baylor plays identical). Current equals legacy on 1.7% of plays, so the\n  2024 model backfill happened. Consumed by PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA Phase 7.\n\n- EPA source comparison done 2026-09-13 in PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA (Phases 6 and 7).\n  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. ~~Fix `load_snapshot.py`~~ **Fixed 2026-09-22** (PR #4): the load merges by primary key\n   and never deletes. The 12,750 Mac-only rows erased by the old load were restored from\n   the pre-load backup. Real dry run on the Mac now reports \"keeps 6,483 / 6,267 local-only\".\n2. ~~Windows load~~ **DONE 2026-09-22.** Windows pulled PR #4 and loaded the Mac's\n   export: **+6,483 (2024) and +6,267 (2025) `pff_premium` rows**, everything else 0,\n   exactly as the dry run predicted. Windows now holds **4,517 video_plays** rows for the\n   first time. **Both machines are current in both directions** — Windows has the Mac's\n   video plays, the Mac has Windows' 2026 season. The round trip is proven in practice,\n   not just in tests.\n3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n4. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n5. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun.\n\n## Gotchas from the first real exchange\n- **A snapshot is not the whole truth for a season.** The original load deleted each\n  season before inserting, which erased 12,750 Mac-only rows the Windows snapshot did\n  not carry. The pre-load backup is what saved them. The load now merges by primary key\n  and deletes nothing (PR #4). Never reintroduce a delete \"to keep it clean\".\n- Read the dry run before the real load: it prints rows added and local-only rows kept,\n  which is exactly the number the old behaviour would have destroyed.\n\n## Open questions\n- None waiting on Eric.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Windows `git pull` may print \"failed to delete .git/worktrees/pff-db-off-drive\": Drive\n  locks the stale folder. Harmless, answer `n`. Clean with Drive paused, then `git worktree prune`.\n- A load never deletes, so a row removed upstream lingers locally. Harmless today: the\n  pipeline's own upserts never delete either.\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"35ad60a3-9738-406d-a871-0dbbc0cf3ebe","timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:39:48.793Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"AGENTS.md\nCLAUDE.md\n     228 AGENTS.md\n      96 docs/STATUS.md\n     324 total\n2026-09-22-mac-snapshot-load-restore.md\n2026-09-22-db-off-drive-and-parquet-snapshots.md\n# STATUS\n\n## Current state (2026-09-22)\n- **The DB no longer lives in the repo.** `src/db.py` resolves it from **`$PFF_DB`**\n  (Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pff-data\\pff.db`), falling back to `data/pff.db` when unset,\n  so the Mac is unchanged until it sets the variable. Cause: `~/Desktop/DEV` is a two-way\n  Google Drive mirror and Drive re-uploads and **locks** the 542 MB file on every write.\n  `GoogleDriveFS.exe` held it open against a running pull. PR #1.\n- **2026 pulled** (`run_pipeline.py --season 2026`): 1,614 games, 16,572 grades,\n  1,252,863 stats, 39,960 premium; graded weeks 0-3. Baylor: 79 players over its 3\n  played games, 17,215 snaps. Week 4 is 2026-09-26, so 3 games is complete, not a gap.\n- **Machines now exchange Parquet, not databases** (PR #2). `scripts/export_snapshot.py`\n  and `scripts/load_snapshot.py`, one file per table per season on Drive plus a\n  manifest. The whole 612 MB DB is **40 MB** of Parquet; all of 2026 is 6 MB. A full\n  snapshot of 2023-2026 is on Drive now, so the Mac can catch up without touching the API.\n- **Mac loaded the snapshot 2026-09-22 18:15** and matches it (22 files, all counts equal;\n  2026 checked row by row). Load bug found, data restored and the script fixed the same night (PR #4).\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n- All 12 PFF API specs saved to `docs/swagger/` (2026-09-13). Eight were new; master-data\n  and grades-feeds were refreshed (both only gained endpoints). The key downloads specs\n  directly: `GET /doc/swagger/<slug>.yaml` with the Bearer JWT.\n- PFF EPA located and verified (2026-09-13): `/v1/video/ncaa/games/{id}/plays` carries\n  `expected_points_added` and `expected_points_added_legacy`, 100% play coverage on\n  Baylor 2024-2026 and six random non-Baylor 2025 games.\n- Video plays ingested for all 25 Baylor 2024-2025 games (2026-09-13): `pff_premium`\n  category `video_plays`, 4,517 rows (both offences), zero missing EPA.\n  `scripts/pull_video_plays.py --season 2024 --season 2025`. Season and week come\n  from the games table: a bowl game's rows carry week \"BG\". Pre-change backup:\n  `data/pff_before_video_plays_20260913_204343.db`.\n- Full 2024 and 2025 seasons pulled (2026-09-13): 285,070 and 290,427 plays plus the\n  games lists, `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py`. Verified against the per-game pull\n  (all 2,215 Baylor plays identical). Current equals legacy on 1.7% of plays, so the\n  2024 model backfill happened. Consumed by PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA Phase 7.\n\n- EPA source comparison done 2026-09-13 in PlayCalls_SuccessRate_EPA (Phases 6 and 7).\n  Decision (Eric): EPA (PFF current) is the EPA source going forward.\n\n## Next\n1. ~~Fix `load_snapshot.py`~~ **Fixed 2026-09-22** (PR #4): the load merges by primary key\n   and never deletes. The 12,750 Mac-only rows erased by the old load were restored from\n   the pre-load backup. Real dry run on the Mac now reports \"keeps 6,483 / 6,267 local-only\".\n2. ~~Windows load~~ **DONE 2026-09-22.** Windows pulled PR #4 and loaded the Mac's\n   export: **+6,483 (2024) and +6,267 (2025) `pff_premium` rows**, everything else 0,\n   exactly as the dry run predicted. Windows now holds **4,517 video_plays** rows for the\n   first time. **Both machines are current in both directions** — Windows has the Mac's\n   video plays, the Mac has Windows' 2026 season. The round trip is proven in practice,\n   not just in tests.\n3. Pull 2026 weekly with `scripts/pull_season_video_plays.py --season 2026 --refresh`, so\n   MatchupAnalysis opponent profiles can quote EPA (PFF current) instead of CFBD PPA.\n4. Re-run `--season 2026` weekly during the season; each run adds the graded week.\n5. After the 2026 season, a full 2026 pull for the PlayCalls Phase 7 rerun.\n\n## Gotchas from the first real exchange\n- **A snapshot is not the whole truth for a season.** The original load deleted each\n  season before inserting, which erased 12,750 Mac-only rows the Windows snapshot did\n  not carry. The pre-load backup is what saved them. The load now merges by primary key\n  and deletes nothing (PR #4). Never reintroduce a delete \"to keep it clean\".\n- Read the dry run before the real load: it prints rows added and local-only rows kept,\n  which is exactly the number the old behaviour would have destroyed.\n\n## Open questions\n- None waiting on Eric.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Windows `git pull` may print \"failed to delete .git/worktrees/pff-db-off-drive\": Drive\n  locks the stale folder. Harmless, answer `n`. Clean with Drive paused, then `git worktree prune`.\n- A load never deletes, so a row removed upstream lingers locally. Harmless today: the\n  pipeline's own upserts never delete either.\n- The Mac's plain `python3` has no `duckdb`. Use `~/.local/bin/uv run --with-requirements requirements.txt --with pyarrow python ...`.\n- The season feed is about 2.5 GB decoded; stream it (ijson), never `response.json()`.\n- `season_plays.to_frame` needs `dtype=object`, or gappy int columns land as `\"2.0\"`/`\"nan\"`.\n- Bowl-week rows carry week \"BG\"; take season and week from the games list.\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"148b8ac4-1c07-4317-a6f6-932ea3d21267","session_id":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","sessionKind":"bg"