"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","sessionId":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","version":"2.1.280","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"046edbf2-c234-4f21-8662-e46b8e61a545","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5006fe82-af7e-4da5-9995-ef680c5b9f3a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# PFF Data Project — Agent Guide\n\nThis file is the canonical project memory for any AI coding agent working in this\nrepo. It is mirrored verbatim into `AGENTS.md` so OpenAI Codex (and any other\nagent that reads `AGENTS.md`) gets the same context. A pre-commit hook in\n`.githooks/pre-commit` blocks commits where the two files diverge.\n\nIf you edit one, edit both. See \"Keeping CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md in sync\" below.\n\n---\n\n## What this project is\n\nA standalone Python data pipeline that pulls Pro Football Focus (PFF) game and\nplayer data into a local **DuckDB** database for Baylor University Football\nanalysis. Scope is **Baylor + every Big 12 team + non-conference opponents** for\nthe **current season plus two prior**.\n\nThe DB *is* the deliverable. There are no dashboards in this repo. Downstream\nconsumers — Power BI, Jupyter notebooks, and a future athlete management system\n(AMS) project that will unify PFF with Catapult GPS, VALD ForceDecks, and Perch\nVBT data — own visualization and cross-domain joins.\n\n## Sister pipelines (do not modify from here)\n\n- **VALD ForceDecks (CMJ/IMTP):** `..\\..\\ForcePlate_DecisionSystem` — the\n  architectural template this project mirrors.\n- **Catapult GPS:** `..\\..\\DataBase_GPS_Reporting`\n- **Perch VBT:** not yet built.\n\nThe pattern across all of them is: per-domain Python pipeline → per-domain DB →\nfuture AMS layer unions them on `(athlete_id, source_system, pulled_at)`.\n\n## Tech stack\n\n- Python 3.12+\n- `duckdb`, `requests`, `python-dotenv`, `PyJWT`, `pyyaml`, `pandas`, `pytest`\n- No web framework, no ORM, no dashboard libs — keep it lean\n\n## Layout\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JR98g4fpPMxucFDmHXGdnJ"}]},"uuid":"3d9e0623-dd74-4b77-99ad-2f713a304ba7","timestamp":"2026-09-23T12:39:54.827Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# PFF Data Project — Agent Guide\n\nThis file is the canonical project memory for any AI coding agent working in this\nrepo. It is mirrored verbatim into `AGENTS.md` so OpenAI Codex (and any other\nagent that reads `AGENTS.md`) gets the same context. A pre-commit hook in\n`.githooks/pre-commit` blocks commits where the two files diverge.\n\nIf you edit one, edit both. See \"Keeping CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md in sync\" below.\n\n---\n\n## What this project is\n\nA standalone Python data pipeline that pulls Pro Football Focus (PFF) game and\nplayer data into a local **DuckDB** database for Baylor University Football\nanalysis. Scope is **Baylor + every Big 12 team + non-conference opponents** for\nthe **current season plus two prior**.\n\nThe DB *is* the deliverable. There are no dashboards in this repo. Downstream\nconsumers — Power BI, Jupyter notebooks, and a future athlete management system\n(AMS) project that will unify PFF with Catapult GPS, VALD ForceDecks, and Perch\nVBT data — own visualization and cross-domain joins.\n\n## Sister pipelines (do not modify from here)\n\n- **VALD ForceDecks (CMJ/IMTP):** `..\\..\\ForcePlate_DecisionSystem` — the\n  architectural template this project mirrors.\n- **Catapult GPS:** `..\\..\\DataBase_GPS_Reporting`\n- **Perch VBT:** not yet built.\n\nThe pattern across all of them is: per-domain Python pipeline → per-domain DB →\nfuture AMS layer unions them on `(athlete_id, source_system, pulled_at)`.\n\n## Tech stack\n\n- Python 3.12+\n- `duckdb`, `requests`, `python-dotenv`, `PyJWT`, `pyyaml`, `pandas`, `pytest`\n- No web framework, no ORM, no dashboard libs — keep it lean\n\n## Layout\n(eval):1: ===== not found","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"046edbf2-c234-4f21-8662-e46b8e61a545","session_id":"45c8cd30-7236-4eb5-ad13-a4c167daef8d","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Football/PFF_Data_Project","ses